Ok here's a test unit case (based on framework unit test)

Add these 2 relations in data/ar/OrderItem.php

``` php
    public function getOrderItemCompositeWithJoin()
    {
        return $this->hasOne(OrderItem::className(), ['item_id' => 'item_id', 'order_id' => 'order_id' ])
                ->joinWith('item');
    }

    public function getOrderItemCompositeNoJoin()
    {
        return $this->hasOne(OrderItem::className(), ['item_id' => 'item_id', 'order_id' => 'order_id' ]);
    }
```

Then add the folowing test case in framework/db/ActiveRecordTest.php

``` php
public function testFindCompositeWithJoin()
    {
        /* @var $orderItem OrderItem */
        $orderItem = OrderItem::findOne([1, 1]);

        $orderItemNoJoin = $orderItem->orderItemCompositeNoJoin;
        $this->assertInstanceOf('yiiunit\data\ar\OrderItem', $orderItemNoJoin);

        $orderItemWithJoin = $orderItem->orderItemCompositeWithJoin;
        $this->assertInstanceOf('yiiunit\data\ar\OrderItem', $orderItemWithJoin);
    }
```

Running the test will pass the first asset while the second will fail

I also stumbled upon this bug. Rather rare case with composite key and join with IN condition.

Would adding this to `QueryBuilder->buildCompositeInCondition()` be too simplistic?

```
if ( ($pos = strpos($column, '.')) !== false ) {
    $column = substr($column, $pos+1);
}
```

Or adding something like this to `ActiveRelationTrait->filterByModels()`

```
            // composite keys
            foreach ($models as $model) {
                $v = [];
                foreach ($this->link as $attribute => $link) {
                    $t = $this->prefixKeyColumns([$attribute]);
                    $v[$t[0]] = $model[$link];
                }
                $values[] = $v;
            }
```

@airmoi Did you find a generic workaround?

Same issue:

```
$attributes = $this->prefixKeyColumns($attributes);
...
// composite keys
foreach ($models as $model) {
    $v = [];
    foreach ($this->link as $attribute => $link) {
        $v[$attribute] = $model[$link];
    }
    $values[] = $v;
}
...
$this->andWhere(['in', $attributes, array_unique($values, SORT_REGULAR)]);
```

I think $attribute should be mapped to prefixed attribute.

